# Blessings Wall — approved wishes, pipe-separated
# Format per line: NN|date|name|message
#   NN      : two-digit id, zero-padded
#   date    : YYYY-MM-DD
#   name    : visitor's display name (1–40 chars)
#   message : blessing / wish (1–280 chars)
# Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# To add a new entry, the simplest path is:
#  1. Visitor submits form on /comment/
#  2. You receive a Web3Forms email
#  3. Click the "Approve" link (a pre-filled GitHub Issue)
#  4. Edit if you want, submit the Issue
#  5. The .github/workflows/approve-blessing.yml action appends a new line and closes the Issue
#
# Manual addition: edit this file directly, commit, push.
